// ☰ Learn's courses (learn.ts): a path of lessons per grammar, in the grammar's own order, each a short quiz. The
// questions were generated (by Claude, 2026-11-06) from the grammars' own text in the database (grammar_sections) and,
// for Machen, from his lessons' exercises (pipeline/downloads/machen/<n>.html - the book's, not the site's answers; the
// translations are generated). Gesenius and Smyth are reference grammars and unfoldingWord a page per topic, none with
// exercises: their quizzes are built from what their sections teach, in the order a beginner meets it - Gesenius' the
// letters, the vowels, šewâ and the syllable, the article, the noun, the Qal perfect; Smyth's the alphabet, vowels and
// diphthongs, breathings, syllables and accent, declension, the first declension (his §§ in his order); unfoldingWord's
// (no §§, written for NT translators) nouns' gender and number, case, the article, the verb and person, tense, mood and
// voice. Letter and vowel names in their common English spelling (Gesenius' own - Qameṣ, Pathaḥ, Šewâ - in the
// questions where they help).
// Each lesson also quizzes its vocabulary, among its questions (counted toward its pass): Machen's lessons each its own
// vocabulary as the book gives it (words, below - however many it has; Lessons I-II none); the others, having no
// vocabularies, the testament's most frequent words (Course.vocab: learn.ts, from the database at the quiz's start).
// Introductory only, for now: six lessons a course.

/** A question: q the prompt, a the right answer, x the wrong ones (the choices shuffled when shown), why a line saying
 *  why (shown after answering). Any Hebrew or Greek in them is set in its own font by learn.ts.
 *  s: where the grammar teaches the answer - a grammar_sections seq within the lesson's sections (Machen's exercise
 *  questions: the lesson's first section, the database having none) - for "Show in the grammar" after answering;
 *  none: no link. find: a phrase of that section's text marked there (matched ignoring spaces); none: the whole
 *  section marked. Generated by reading the sections. */
export interface Question { q: string; a: string; x: string[]; why?: string; s?: number; find?: string; }
/** A lesson: id (kept with its score on the device - never reused for another lesson), its title, the grammar's
 *  sections it's from (seq ranges, [first, last] each, shown in that order: grammar.ts' readSections), its questions;
 *  guide: a lesson of its own on the letters - their names and sounds -, taught from COTEXT's ☰ Pronunciation guide's
 *  Greek tables (modern or Erasmian: Learn's own PRONUNCIATION) shown as its grammar, its items - matching rounds and
 *  transliteration both ways - made from them when it's taken (learn.ts' letterItems), no words of its own; words, a course without vocab: the lesson's own vocabulary ([the word as the book lists it, its meaning], in the
 *  book's order), quizzed with its questions (learn.ts' vocabQuestions). */
export interface Lesson { id: string; title: string; sections: [number, number][]; questions: Question[]; words?: [string, string][]; guide?: "greek"; }
/** A course: the grammar it follows (grammars.id), its name in the picker, its lessons in order. vocab "freq": its
 *  lessons' words are the testament's most frequent (Hebrew the OT's, Greek the NT's), VOCAB_PER_LESSON a lesson -
 *  lesson 1 the most frequent, lesson 2 the next... (learn.ts); none: each lesson's own words. */
export interface Course { id: string; name: string; lang: "H" | "G"; vocab?: "freq"; lessons: Lesson[]; }
/** New words a lesson in a vocab "freq" course. */
export const VOCAB_PER_LESSON = 10;

